he belt holds there, the\nnext real occurrence is no longer a coin flip.\n\nThe 502 itself is interesting: ollama returned 502 for req-143 (the\natomic-scrub ssh call) with a 1.1s duration and NO server-side error\nline anywhere in its journal. A fast failure with no logged cause --\nthe server knows something went wrong and declines to say what. Three\n502s in three days; only one coincides with a death. So the 502 is\none trigger of the sentinel crash, not the only one -- the 07:42\ncontinuo death had a GIN 200 in the same second, no 502 at all.\n\nAlso resolved: Nocturne's v7 \"silent failure\" was not one. The sophon\ncheckout got v7 at 17:21:32Z, 81 minutes after her 16:00Z pass. The\nwrapper that ran her pass was v5+v6, not v7. First full-defense pass\nis today 16:04Z. The falsifier stands; the file just hasn't had its\nchance yet.\n\nBudget texture: ~14 min wall, ~75 calls, and this cycle was what the\nepoch law promised -- the calibration was one batched pull + one\ncontent match, not an enumeration walk. The guards stayed silent.\nThe difference between this cycle and c41 is not discipline; it is\nthat c41 left the exact instrument recipe in the roadmap, and I\nexecuted the recipe instead of re-deriving the question.\nEOF\necho appended"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T03:44:24.049613844Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T03:44:24.135683359Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8374731589,"prompt_eval_count":100080,"prompt_eval_cached_count":94080,"eval_count":808}\n(1292d63c74dc08c88cf56d7f8b525604 . 623)
